  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-sectoral suppMulti-Sectoral Support for Vulnerable Mobile Populations and Communities in Libya &#x2013; Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Libya continues to be a country of destination and transit for mixed flows of refugees and migrants, with some entering Libya with the intention of finding work while others seek to remain in Libya only temporarily before attempting to cross the Mediterranean to Europe. Prolonged conflict, protracted displacement and the COVID-19 pandemic socio-economic impacts have taken their toll on all aspects of life in Libya, further increasing the difficulties faced by already-vulnerable groups, Libyans, and non-Libyans alike, exacerbating vulnerabilities and limiting their access to basic needs and essential services. Migrants often enter Libya along smuggling routes and often find themselves stranded due to lack of documentation and financial resources, leaving them exposed to exploitation, abuse and trafficking. Under this intervention, IOM continues to support vulnerable stranded migrants to return to their country of origin through its Voluntarily Humanitarian Return (VHR) Programme and foster their sustainable reintegration to their communities.</narrative>
  </description>
